  nonce: 027e  # 027e
  message: "Additional investigation from 2026-04-10 session: Confirmed the pattern in prometheus web/api/v1/api.go. Lines 384-415 declare 'wrap' and 'wrapAgent' as closure variables inside Register(). Lines 416-450 use them as r.Get('/query', wrapAgent(api.query)). The route resolver already resolves api.query → API.query correctly. The missing piece is specifically: when a route handler argument is a call_expression (e.g., wrapAgent(...)), detect that the callee is a closure variable, and emit a wraps/middleware_of edge from the closure to the inner handler argument. Implementation approach: (1) in _extract_go_var_types, detect func-typed variables from short_var_declarations where RHS is a func_literal, (2) in the route handler extraction (around go.py:3174), when handler arg is a call_expression whose callee matches a func-typed local var, emit a wraps edge. This doesn't require modeling the closure body — just the wrapping relationship."  # 027e
